      <div type="clause" n="37">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Af">Af</ref> 37</head>
        <ab type="selectedText" xml:lang="und">Gif mon wille of boldgetale in oðer boldgetæl hlaford secan, do ðæt mid ðæs ealdormonnes gewitnesse, þe he ær \in/ his scire folgode.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en">If someone wishes [to leave] from his district to seek a lord in another district, let him do so with the knowledge of the ealdorman, to whom he was subject before in his shire.</ab>
        <ab type="secondTranslation" xml:lang="en">If a man wishes [to go] from one district, to seek service in another, he shall do it with the cognisance of the ealdorman, to whose jurisdiction he has previously been subject.</ab>
        <ab type="supplementaryText" xml:lang="und">XXXIIII. Gif mon of boldgetale wille in oðer boldgetæl hlaford secan, dò ðæt mid ðæs ealdormonnes gewitnesse, ðe he ǽr on his scire folgode.</ab>
      </div>
